Usage: runner [options] tests...
test-unit options:
    -h, --help                       Display this help.
>    -s, --seed SEED                  Sets random seed
>    -v, --verbose                    Verbose. Show progress processing files.
>    -n, --name PATTERN               Filter test method names on pattern: /REGEXP/, !/REGEXP/ or STRING
>        --test-order=random|alpha|sorted|nosort
status line options:
        --jobs-status [TYPE]         Show status of jobs every file; Disabled when --jobs isn't specified.
        --color[=WHEN]               colorize the output.  WHEN defaults to 'always'
                                     or can be 'never' or 'auto'.
        --tty[=WHEN]                 force to output tty control.  WHEN defaults to 'yes'
                                     or can be 'no'.
parallel test options:
    -j, --jobs N                     Allow run tests with N jobs at once
        --worker-timeout=N           Timeout workers not responding in N seconds
        --separate                   Restart job process after one testcase has done
        --retry                      Retry running testcase when --jobs specified
        --no-retry                   Disable --retry
        --ruby VAL                   Path to ruby which is used at -j option
                                     Also used as EnvUtil.rubybin by some assertion methods
        --timetable-data=FILE        Path to timetable data
statistics options:
        --longest=N                  Show longest N tests
        --most-asserted=N            Show most asserted N tests
skipping options:
    -q, --hide-skip                  Hide skipped tests
        --show-skip                  Show skipped tests
globbing options:
    -B, --base-directory DIR         Base directory to glob.
>    -x, --exclude REGEXP             Exclude test files on pattern.
output options:
        --stderr-on-failure          Use stderr to print failure messages
        --stdout-on-failure          Use stdout to print failure messages
                                     (default)
repeat options:
        --repeat-count=NUM           Number of times to repeat
load path options:
    -Idirectory                      Add library load path
GC options:
        --[no-]gc-stress             Set GC.stress as true
        --[no-]gc-compact            GC.compact every time
excludes options:
    -X, --excludes-dir DIRECTORY     Directory name of exclude files
timeout options:
>        --timeout-scale, --subprocess-timeout-scale NUM
                                     Scale timeout
Launchable options:
        --launchable-test-reports=PATH
                                     Report test results in Launchable JSON format